Negative control for form-cutover.test.ts — the icon seam.

Drops the wrapper's `provideFormIcon(Icon)` call, so `@upmind/ui`'s engine falls
back to its render-nothing default and every engine glyph disappears: the
FormField label icon, the tooltip trigger, and the leading icon inside the
control. Nothing else changes — the country seam, the host binding and the model
round-trip are untouched.

The unused `provideFormIcon` and `Icon` imports go with it. Left behind they trip
`noUnusedLocals` and the mutant grades TYPECHECK instead of the assertion.

Expected: the two assertions under "the wrapper's icon reaches the engine" that
read the wrapper path go red — "draws the label icon and the tooltip trigger the
uischema names" and "draws the leading icon inside the field". The paired
bare-engine control, "draws no glyph at all on a host nobody supplied an icon
to", must stay GREEN; that pairing is what separates a real seam assertion from
one passing on ambient state. Both country assertions stay green.

